{
  "description": "Integrate QuestDB as a supported BenchBox platform. QuestDB is a high-performance\nopen-source time-series database (Apache 2.0 license) optimized for fast ingestion\nand SQL queries over time-series data. It has strong adoption in financial services,\nIoT, and observability use cases (14K+ GitHub stars).\n\nTechnical fit analysis:\n- PostgreSQL wire protocol support (port 8812) - can use psycopg2/asyncpg\n- Standard SQL support with time-series extensions (SAMPLE BY, LATEST ON)\n- SQLGlot may need custom dialect or 'postgres' with adjustments\n- High-performance InfluxDB Line Protocol (ILP) ingestion endpoint\n- REST API for queries and data import (CSV upload)\n- Columnar storage with SIMD-optimized execution\n\nStrategic value:\n- Fills gap in time-series database coverage (alongside TimescaleDB, InfluxDB)\n- Enables benchmarking time-series specific workloads and ingestion rates\n- Growing adoption in real-time analytics and financial data scenarios\n- Complements existing OLAP platforms with specialized time-series focus\n\nNote: QuestDB's strengths are in time-series workloads; TPC-H/TPC-DS may not\nshowcase its optimal use case. Consider time-series specific benchmarks as\nfuture enhancement.",
